//! ggx_albedo.rs: the directional albedo of the GGX lobe under Schlick's
//! Fresnel, E_s(mu) = F0 A(r, mu) + (1 - F0) B(r, mu), tabulated over the
//! roughness r and the cosine mu with the cosine-weighted average of every
//! row, for the coat's pigment factor (1 - E_s(mu_o)) (1 - E_s(mu_i)) /
//! (1 - Ebar_s) (HW3 handout, the Cook shading model's coat; HW4 handout,
//! the BSDF); the twin of the C++ kit's `src/ggx_albedo.h`. Given complete
//! in the HW3 kit, so that a coat written to the handout gives the
//! reference's numbers. Declare it in `main.rs` beside the other modules
//! (`mod ggx_albedo;`). Generated by tools/ggx_albedo.py, which also
//! reports the lookup's largest errors: do not edit.
